+# What the estate actually runs, and what holds it
+
+Generated by `bin/idp-estate-audit` at 2026-08-31T10:52:27Z in uk-london-1. Rerun it any time; nothing here is typed by hand.
+
+Of 142 resources running in the tenancy, **53 are described by Terraform**, 41 are made by something that is, and **48 exist in no repository at all**. That last number is the work: until it is zero, a fresh estate cannot be rebuilt from git.
+
+## Coverage by resource type
+
+| Resource type | Running | In Terraform | Made by a managed thing | To codify |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| BootVolume | 2 | 0 | 2 | 0 |
+| Bucket | 3 | 0 | 0 | 3 |
+| ClustersCluster | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
+| Compartment | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 |
+| CustomerDnsZone | 6 | 0 | 6 | 0 |
+| DnsResolver | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 |
+| DnsView | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 |
+| Group | 3 | 0 | 0 | 3 |
+| Instance | 2 | 0 | 2 | 0 |
+| InternetGateway | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
+| Key | 4 | 1 | 0 | 3 |
+| LoadBalancer | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 |
+| NatGateway | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
+| NetworkSecurityGroup | 5 | 5 | 0 | 0 |
+| Policy | 8 | 6 | 0 | 2 |
+| PrivateIp | 5 | 0 | 5 | 0 |
+| PublicIp | 3 | 0 | 3 | 0 |
+| RouteTable | 4 | 3 | 0 | 1 |
+| SecurityList | 3 | 3 | 0 | 0 |
+| ServiceGateway | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
+| Subnet | 5 | 5 | 0 | 0 |
+| TagDefault | 2 | 0 | 0 | 2 |
+| TagNamespace | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 |
+| User | 4 | 0 | 0 | 4 |
+| Vault | 2 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
+| VaultSecret | 51 | 24 | 0 | 27 |
+| Vcn | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
+| Vnic | 4 | 0 | 4 | 0 |
+| Volume | 16 | 0 | 16 | 0 |
+
+### Why the middle column is not work
+
+- **BootVolume** — the OKE worker pool makes these with its nodes
+- **CustomerDnsZone** — OCI private DNS for a managed VCN
+- **DnsResolver** — OCI private DNS for a managed VCN
+- **DnsView** — OCI private DNS for a managed VCN
+- **Instance** — a worker node from the managed pool
+- **LoadBalancer** — answered by the cluster for a Service of type LoadBalancer
+- **PrivateIp** — assigned to a managed vnic
+- **PublicIp** — assigned to a managed node or load balancer
+- **Vnic** — attached by the worker pool when a node comes up
+- **Volume** — the block-volume CSI driver makes one per persistent claim
+
+Those are recreated by whatever owns them when the estate is rebuilt. What is *not* recreated is the data on them, which is why `bin/idp-estate-backup` exists.
+
+## The codify list
+
+Every resource below exists because someone made it by hand. Each one is a Terraform block that has to be written before step 4 can stand up a second estate.
+
+| Resource type | Name | State |
+|---|---|---|
+| Bucket | estate-drill-receipts | active |
+| Bucket | estate-shop-backups | active |
+| Bucket | estate-tofu-state | active |
+| Compartment | estate | ACTIVE |
+| Group | All Domain Users | None |
+| Group | estate-operators | None |
+| Group | `estate-provers` | None |
+| Key | RSA wrapping key | PENDING_DELETION |
+| Key | RSA wrapping key | ENABLED |
+| Key | estate-secrets | PENDING_DELETION |
+| Policy | Tenant Admin Policy | ACTIVE |
+| Policy | estate-operators-manage-estate | ACTIVE |
+| RouteTable | Default Route Table for oke-tiafzl | AVAILABLE |
+| TagDefault | createdby | None |
